  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Word2Vec** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef nlp_word2vec(target_embed: list, context_embed: list, negative_embeds: list) -> float:\n    v_t = np.array(target_embed, dtype=float)\n    v_c = np.array(context_embed, dtype=float)\n    neg = np.array(negative_embeds, dtype=float)\n    pos_loss = np.log(1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-np.clip(np.dot(v_c, v_t), -20.0, 20.0))))\n    neg_loss = np.sum(np.log(1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(np.clip(neg @ v_t, -20.0, 20.0)))))\n    return round(float(-(pos_loss + neg_loss)), 6)\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
